    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The record for KMD holds two facts and a verdict. The facts are that it is a Danish public-sector incumbent and that it is Japanese-owned; the verdict is priority 9, do not pitch. Its tool column reads not researched, so no platform, no open-source posture and no slot-occupancy assessment exist for this row.\n\nBoth recorded facts point the same way under the screen's criteria as they are applied elsewhere in the corpus. Public-sector incumbency delivers access but not partnership fit \u2014 the pattern named explicitly for the Sopra Steria entries \u2014 and ownership outside the region is treated as disqualifying even for firms with strong local benches. Neither inference is spelled out here, though, which is why this row should be read as thinly evidenced rather than firmly settled.\n\nThe practical value of the entry is as a placeholder with a known gap: if Denmark is ever worked seriously, KMD is the incumbent to understand for market context, and the first thing to do is research the stack that was never recorded.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- KMD (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Danish public-sector incumbent, Japanese-owned.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:26:08.603859Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:26:08.603864Z"
    }
